WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.200
To enforce standards, institutions rely on
research ethics committees.

2
00:00:05.540 --> 00:00:09.780
These formal bodies review project
proposals and oversee investigations when

3
00:00:09.820 --> 00:00:12.140
deviations in integrity are reported.

4
00:00:12.660 --> 00:00:16.580
Formal investigations into research
misconduct are guided by the principles of

5
00:00:16.620 --> 00:00:20.520
integrity and fairness as defined by the
European Code of Conduct.

6
00:00:20.780 --> 00:00:23.400
Investigations operate under strict
parameters.

7
00:00:23.560 --> 00:00:27.220
They must be comprehensive, conducted
expediently, and remain fiercely

8
00:00:27.260 --> 00:00:28.640
objective throughout the process.

9
00:00:28.680 --> 00:00:32.240
The process adheres to a foundational
legal standard.

10
00:00:32.500 --> 00:00:36.360
Any individual accused of misconduct is
presumed innocent until the evidence

11
00:00:36.400 --> 00:00:40.640
proves otherwise. Furthermore, all parties
involved in an investigation are

12
00:00:40.680 --> 00:00:44.780
strictly required to declare any potential
conflicts of interest immediately.

13
00:00:45.120 --> 00:00:49.680
Institutional reproducibility relies
entirely on standardizing compliance

14
00:00:49.720 --> 00:00:53.700
frameworks and architecting robust,
transparent data ecosystems.

15
00:00:53.740 --> 00:00:58.100
Maintaining the accuracy of the scientific
record is an active,

16
00:00:58.140 --> 00:01:02.140
ongoing operational commitment required by
all researchers and their

17
00:01:02.180 --> 00:01:03.180
institutions.
